CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ requires over variable template: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [temp.constr.atomic]/1: a constructor template constrained by a
requires-clause naming a MEMBER variable template whose default
argument refers to the ENCLOSING class template's parameter
(`template <typename, typename = _Tp> static constexpr bool ok`).
Evaluating the atom must install the declaration's parameter mapping;
without it the atom's typecheck threw and the candidate was silently
removed (gcc-16 <optional>'s converting constructor,
__not_constructing_bool_from_optional).  Runtime-verified g++ 13 /
clang++ 18.
